On 6/2/26 3:49 PM, sashiko-bot@kernel.org wrote:
> Thank you for your contribution! Sashiko AI review found 2 potential issue(s) to consider:
> 
> Pre-existing issues:
> - [Critical] Generic BPF map iterators bypass BPF_F_RDONLY_PROG and map->frozen protections.
> - [High] Incomplete fix for exclusive map security bypass via dynamic attach points
These are two pre-existing issues and not relevant for the integrity of signed loaders
which this patch series addresses.

The exclusivity guarantee ("only the hash-matching program may touch this map") as a
concept outside of signing may be worth to fix the sk_storage.. The iterators one being
able to write into frozen/RDONLY_PROG maps is an issue as well given verifier treats
these as known constants. I'll add them to my todo list.
